BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 317.77 Tm (The first trap is the cash hole that opens before a single dollar comes back. Casey Gard walks through the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 302.55 Tm (arithmetic: 500 cases at $10,000 each means $5 million laid out up front, and Dodd-Frank-era limits keep) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 287.32 Tm (banks from lending against contingency assets, which is why firms land at funders' doors [g66VtR5b5gQ @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 272.10 Tm (00:22:25]. Ted Farrell itemizes the hard costs behind that number, with $400 to $500 filing fees, medical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 256.87 Tm (record orders, and nurse review pushing workup into the thousands per case, so that 10,000 clients at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 241.65 Tm ($3,000 each becomes roughly $30 million [gdDT2WSKYs0 @ 00:10:38]. Farrell mocks the advertising pitch) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 226.42 Tm (directly: "at 3,000 bucks a pop you know just come up with 15 million bucks and you too could you know be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 211.20 Tm (doing those cases" [gdDT2WSKYs0 @ 00:09:21]. Dave Kirsty names the two internal gaps that turn that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 195.97 Tm (burn into a crisis: poor budgeting and no partner-compensation mechanism for cases carried on risk, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 180.75 Tm (problem that bites because funders cap their commitment at 50 to 70 percent of the budget [fTOe5KR6QSE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 165.52 Tm (@ 00:14:45]. Camp Lejeune adds a timing drag on top, since every claim requires an individual) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 150.30 Tm (administrative process before filing, stretching the period in which cash is out and nothing is returning.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 135.07 Tm (Valuation errors are the second recurring loss. Adam Rosen of Rocade, an ex-Ashcraft & Gerel MDL) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 119.85 Tm (litigator, warns that naive per-plaintiff averaging overvalues "product in place" dockets, and the firms that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 104.62 Tm (lean on it keep refinancing instead of getting paid [Zz1HlCrfQPY @ 00:52:13]. Rocade's fix is to value every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 89.40 Tm (case by injury subtype rather than a settlement average, which is how the shop modeled three separate 3M) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 74.17 Tm (grids in 2020, and Rosen's blunt summary is "Data is everything," meaning fee splits, expenses and surgery) Tj ET
