BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Detail: Rollover equity and vesting substitute for unenforceable non-competes, and a missing performance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (plan is a 'yellow flag' [Mattern LLC - 8wwcTCIWOXM @ 00:15:04]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 678.55 Tm (The Mattern LLC walkthrough gives the build order. Step one is forming the MSO, 'typically just a Delaware) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (LLC' [8wwcTCIWOXM @ 00:04:03]. Non-legal assets then move across, and the MSO licenses or leases) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (them back under a business services agreement for a monthly fee, with an accounting firm validating) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (fairness; the stated goal is to move as much economics as is defensible, net of attorney compensation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm ([8wwcTCIWOXM @ 00:06:30]. Only then does the investor buy all or part of the MSO, either for partner) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (liquidity or growth capital. Valuation is built vertical by vertical, marketing, HR and so on, and the rules do) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (not require fair market value; it functions as a defense. On fee levels, Rich puts typical cost-plus markups at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (10-15%, and says fee changes should be forward-looking only, with the fairness analysis refreshed; an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (annual cadence 'seems more or less sensible,' though there are no hard and fast rules [5TjsKzLtyc4 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (00:25:36]. The Esquire Bank panel structures the agreement by defining the services, the MSO-owned IP) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (and the resources used, then paying a fixed monthly amount like any vendor, re-evaluated as MSO) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (headcount grows, usually yearly and sometimes sooner [epFmlanyChw @ 00:01:08]. Annual re-pricing is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (the shared default across both camps.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (Because lawyers cannot be bound by non-competes, even in an asset sale, and Josh Port warns there are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm ('no silver bullets,' the deal paper has to do the retention work. The Mattern walkthrough lists the levers:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (rollover equity, equity forfeiture, and five-year vesting of cash, for example returning 60% if a lawyer quits in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (year two [8wwcTCIWOXM @ 00:19:20]. Name, image and likeness licenses are another lever, and the Jon) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (and Marc panel reports these run 'in perpetuity' and can permit AI versions of the founder [U2xFBBUm_IU) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (@ 00:20:06]. Rich flags two drafting traps that show up in investor paper. First, personal liability for unpaid) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (MSO fees should be rewritten as deferred fees [5TjsKzLtyc4 @ 00:42:21]. Second, non-solicitation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (covenants that reach lawyers or clients violate Rule 5.6 and have to come out. Plans cut both ways: an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (investor that arrives without a performance plan is a 'yellow flag,' and a firm that takes money without its own) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (plan faces 'a tremendous amount of pressure' from equity partners to pay it out in compensation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm ([8wwcTCIWOXM @ 00:42:49]. On the exit side, the Jon and Marc panelists say less founder reliance earns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (a higher EBITDA multiple and that a couple of years of track record matters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (Litigation funding has its own mechanics on the same capital map. Bentham's Dave Kirstine sets a $1-1.5M) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (minimum with a $5-15M wheelhouse, wants case value at 8-10x the commitment, and runs intake, NDA, an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (in-person meeting, a non-binding term sheet within about a week, then binding 30-45 day exclusivity) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm ([rQPZlRgHcfE @ 00:11:07]. Much Shelist's Jonathan Friedland lays out the formal market process: rifled) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (rather than shotgun outreach, an anonymized teaser, CA, CIM, term sheet, diligence, then the funding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (agreement [9teRv9eFpEc @ 00:26:04]. Selectivity is brutal: Hannah Sadler reports about 4 funded per) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (hundreds reviewed, and Statera's Stewart Ackerly prices on a multiple of capital actually drawn, often less) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (than the commitment. Burford's Chris Bogart says Burford funds only 6-8% of the cases it reviews and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (describes the default waterfall: capital back first, then a time-based multiple starting around 0.5x and rising,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm (then a share of net recovery; on $10 million deployed, Burford looks for '$10 million back and then another) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.67 Tm ($5 million' on the time-based leg [1kAfGIkF10g @ 00:27:53]. Bogart reports mid-20s IRRs, ROIC in the 80s) Tj ET
