BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.78 Tm (The ABS failures already on the record cluster around firms that forgot they are law firms. Lynda Shely) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 222.55 Tm (reports that two compliance lawyers have been disciplined and reads that as proof the system works, but the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 207.33 Tm (operator takeaway is that the named ethics officer is the first person exposed when a firm slips) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 192.10 Tm ([OdPOa3osKC0 @ 00:10:44]. Shely also warns against the cheap compliance-lawyer model: the role needs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.88 Tm (management experience, and one person should not be stretched across five to seven firms) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 161.65 Tm ([OdPOa3osKC0 @ 00:19:39]. The sharpest trap hits mass-tort and PI operators, who made up 26 of the 65) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 146.43 Tm (ABS firms counted in the three-year update: a bar complaint is pending over a firm allegedly just referring) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 131.20 Tm (cases out, and Shely states an Arizona lawyer must give substantive input on intake, medical-record review) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.98 Tm (and client communication, so an empty Arizona office funneling cases to Florida is not allowed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 100.75 Tm ([poe1CAsUc4U @ 00:36:28]. On the Law Leaders update, Shely closes with the line every tort aggregator) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 85.53 Tm (should keep in view: this is not a get-rich-quick scheme, even though ER 7.2's elimination now lets Arizona) Tj ET
